All the dotfiles that I need to get up and running. To install just run
the install script in the root directory.

NOTE: on OS X you may need to do the following (hope to automate this later):

- `brew install ctags`
- `brew install hub`

If you want faster searching install the_silver_searcher. Vim should still successfully
load without this installed.
- `brew install the_silver_searcher`

## Git identity

`.gitconfig` only sets `[user] name`. The email lives in two machine-local
files that are NOT committed to this repo:

- `~/.gitconfig.personal` — default email for non-Datadog repos
- `~/.gitconfig.work` — Datadog email, applied via `includeIf` for repos
  under `~/dd/` or `~/go/src/github.com/DataDog/`

Both files are silently skipped if missing, so create only what each machine
needs.

```sh
# Personal email default (every machine)
cat > ~/.gitconfig.personal <<'EOF'
[user]
    email = <personal email>
EOF

# Work email override (work machines only)
cat > ~/.gitconfig.work <<'EOF'
[user]
    email = <work email>
EOF
```

Verify with `git config --show-origin --get user.email` from inside a Datadog
repo (expect `.gitconfig.work`) and from anywhere else (expect
`.gitconfig.personal`).
